{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give SwiftUI views a tracker through the environment, and track what they do with view modifiers."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this module to track events from SwiftUI views on Apple platforms; elsewhere it builds empty."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Set a tracker once, at the root of the views, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and read it in any view below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Environment(\\.tracker)"},{"type":"text","text":". A button’s action can track through it, which a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binding can’t reach, since SwiftUI runs actions on tasks of its own. Until a tracker is set, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"environment’s tracker tracks through the one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.bootstrap"},{"type":"text","text":" made the process’s default, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with none it drops each event, warning once per call site. In a preview it is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.noOp"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a preview tracks nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifiers track through the environment’s tracker, once per trigger, and record the place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they are applied as the call site. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackOnAppear(_:)"},{"text":" tracks each time a view appears,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackOnTap(_:)"},{"text":" each tap beside the view’s own action, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackChange(of:_:)"},{"text":" each new value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreen(_:)"},{"text":" tracks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenViewed"},{"text":" each time the view appears, and puts a tracker enriched","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the screen’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenKey"},{"text":" in the environment inside it, so every event tracked from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"screen carries its name:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftUI","import Traffluent","","@Event","struct CartOpened {}","","@Event","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","}","","struct CartView: View {","    @Environment(\\.tracker) private var tracker","","    var body: some View {","        List {","            Button(\"Check out\") {","                tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3))  \/\/ its record's context[ScreenKey.self] is \"Cart\"","            }","        }","        .trackOnAppear(CartOpened())","    }","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let root = CartView()","    .trackScreen(\"Cart\")  \/\/ tracks ScreenViewed(screen: \"Cart\") each time it appears","    .tracker(tracker)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Apply ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where the screen’s view is placed, as above, not in the view’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a view’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Environment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads the environment around it, which its own body’s modifiers don’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Where UIKit has traits, the environment’s tracker is the same value as UIKit’s trait","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"reference"},{"text":"), so SwiftUI views hosted in UIKit read the scene’s tracker. For UIKit and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"AppKit views, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"To track screens without a modifier on each, see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The guide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers all three frameworks.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"API","type":"heading","text":"API","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s views aren’t there, so their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them for an Apple target. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenKey"},{"text":" build on every platform, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracking plan or a collector off Apple platforms can name them.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Setting-the-tracker","type":"heading","text":"Setting the tracker","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EnvironmentValues.tracker"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.tracker(_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"anchor":"Tracking-from-views","type":"heading","text":"Tracking from views","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.trackOnAppear(_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.trackOnTap(_:)"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.trackChange(of:_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"anchor":"Screens","type":"heading","text":"Screens","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.trackScreen(_:)"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenKey","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"SwiftUITracking","modules":[{"name":"SwiftUITracking"}],"externalID":"SwiftUITracking","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenKey"],"a